  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "MqttDecode_Props",
    "file": "wolfmqtt/src/mqtt_packet.c",
    "description": "Heap OOB read is caused by missing bounds checks in property decoding loop. MqttDecode_Props calls MqttDecode_Vbi(buf, ..., buf_len-(buf-pbuf)) for each property identifier, but it does not first ensure there is any data left in the declared property section (prop_len) and does not consistently constrain reads to prop_len. If prior parsing underflows/over-consumes prop_len (word32) or leaves buf at/near end, loop can still attempt another identifier decode and MqttDecode_Vbi dereferences buf (line 232), producing OOB read.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires an AUTH packet path (via MqttDecode_Auth) where reason code permits properties and attacker-controlled property length/contents are inconsistent. Fuzzer input supplies malformed property bytes so MqttDecode_Auth passes rx_payload+buf_len/props_len into MqttDecode_Props; inside loop, insufficient remaining bytes for next property identifier are not rejected before MqttDecode_Vbi reads first byte. Thus crafted packet with invalid/truncated properties can drive buf past available heap buffer and crash."
  },
